# Copy to frontend/.env.local for local development. In the normal case you
# want this file to set NOTHING -- vite.config.ts proxies /api, /audio and
# /refs to the backend, so api.ts falls back to relative paths and the app
# works from any device on your network with no per-device configuration.
#
# Set VITE_BACKEND_URL only for the dormant Vercel + RunPod split (deployment
# mode 4 in CLAUDE.md), where the frontend and the backend genuinely are
# separate origins and no proxy can bridge them.
#
# Two ways it bites if you set it here:
#   - dev: whatever address you write is the one EVERY visitor calls. Point it
#     at 127.0.0.1 and a phone on the wifi loads the page, then calls its own
#     loopback and finds nothing.
#   - build: the value is BAKED INTO THE BUNDLE. It must be unset when
#     building for LAN or the desktop installer. build.sh handles that -- it
#     stashes .env.local before the frontend build and restores it after.
# VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# Only set in the Vercel project, never locally. Gates the RunPod wake path in
# frontend/api/wake.ts; unset means the app talks to the backend directly.
# VITE_USE_RUNPOD_WAKE=1
